## 6. Failure Handling & Edge Cases

### ⚠️ Loud User Bias
The Synthesizer reports a **"Coverage Score."** The UI visually flags reports where a single participant dominates insight generation to prevent over-indexing on one voice.

### ⚠️ Boring Insights
The Synthesizer applies a **"Novelty Filter"** to highlight contradictions and specific technical friction over broad consensus.

### ⚠️ Diarization Drift
Standard models (WhisperX / Pyannote) frequently "drift" in 60+ minute files. V1 implements:
- **Chunk-Level Re-alignment**, or
- A **UI "nudge"** every 10 minutes of audio to prevent the Auditor from attributing Participant insights to the Interviewer

### ⚠️ Diarization Confusion
If the confidence score for speaker labeling falls **below a set threshold**, the UI highlights speaker names (e.g., in yellow) during the Step-Gate to force manual verification before extraction.

### ⚠️ The "Hallucination of Absence"
To mitigate the risk of missed insights, the Verification Center includes a **"Missing Something?" natural language search bar** — allowing researchers to query the raw transcript directly to surface themes the extraction agent may have overlooked.

### ⚠️ Media Binaries Failure
If FFmpeg / MoviePy is missing, the UI provides a **clear non-technical error** with a text-only fallback.

